      "finding": "subjective/6",
      "takeaway": "Read the run once into plain data, then hand it to one of two renderers.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "`renderStrip` decides which layout you get in two places at once. The surface check at the top only says whether a drawing *could* exist; whether one does is settled by which branch happened to call `track()`, which writes the outer `drawing` as a side effect. The `ended` branch never calls it, so off the terminal an ended run silently falls back to the text layout — the P3 at `mod/strip.ts:290` in this same Dossier is that consequence."
        },
        {
